# A dynamic loop index invalidates every recorded element type

Verifies a write through an index the compiler cannot resolve is treated as an
alias for every slot, so no slot keeps a stale record. Both iterations still
resolve the stored value at runtime and add `10mm + 1mm = 11mm`.

>>> source
let a: int[] = [10mm, 10mm]
let index = 0

for (i in 0..2) {
    print(a[1] + 1mm)
    a[index] = 2cm
}

<<< stdout
11mm
11mm

<<< stderr
